                                "example_id": "8991430b-061b-4039-8b33-16bf66050c84",
                                "sense_id": "a4d5eb4b-fb50-3c8f-8b78-4890df45949a",
                                "text": "Former Premier Hao Pei-tsun (郝柏村), who was the most powerful man in Taiwan's military during the rule of the late President Chiang Ching-kuo (蔣經國), yesterday revealed that Taiwan had long ago acquired the ability to produce nuclear weapons, without actually having launched any test explosions.\n\"Following the success of [Taiwan's] nuclear program, President Chiang openly declared that Taiwan had become a nuclear-capable country, but that it would not bring the research results into production,\" Hao said, speaking to reporters at a book launch for his two-volume work published under the title of Eight-year's diary as the Chief of the General Staff."
                            }
                        ]
